  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Removing the care-team gating fact lets the model invent a permitted clinical access (ReadRecord) by a clinician who has no active care-team membership for the target patient.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing the always-on-audit fact lets the model produce a permitted access (admin ListAudit) with no matching audit entry.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_015_NoPermitWithoutAudit
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_NoPermitWithoutAudit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: Removing the attribution fact lets an audit entry attribute the access to someone other than the actual caller.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_013_AuditShape
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditShape: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AdminOnlyAudit  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AdminOnlyAudit.als
    rationale: Without the admin-only gate on the audit endpoint, a clinical-role caller can be permitted on ListAudit — but Doctor->ListAudit is not in the permission matrix, so LeastPrivilege bites.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditEndpoint
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AdminOnlyAuditEndpoint: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ByteEquivalentDenial  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_ByteEquivalentDenial.als
    rationale: Removing the byte-equivalent-denial fact lets a Denied response and a NotFoundOrDenied response take on different external response shapes, leaking the existence of restricted resources.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_ByteEquivalentDenial
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_ByteEquivalentDenial: FAIL (expected)

